course: dictionary
lesson: 1982
title: Compost: a word with two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Compost is a dark, crumbly mixture made from rotted plant and food waste. The words around it give you clues: «Worms, fungi and bacteria break kitchen scraps down into rich compost». Things that break down and rich mixtures are clues that it is not food for people. It is what scraps turn into when they rot.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The compost feeds the patch next year» still makes sense if you say «The dark, crumbly mixture feeds the patch next year». It makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Compost can also be a verb. To compost is to put peelings and leaves in a heap or bin so they rot. Look at the word endings: composts, composted and composting show it is an action. Compost as a noun is uncountable, so you say some compost, not a compost.
fact: Compost means a dark, crumbly mixture made from rotted plant and food waste.
fact: As a verb, to compost means to put waste such as peelings and leaves in a heap so it rots.
fact: Compost feeds the soil and helps plants grow.
fact: Worms, fungi and bacteria are decomposers: they break down dead plants and food scraps into compost.
fact: Composting helps reduce rubbish, so less waste goes to the general bin.
exercise: «The compost feeds the patch next year.» What does compost do for the patch? | Makes the patch into a pond | Keeps the patch cold all winter | *Feeds the soil so plants can grow | Covers the patch with stones
exercise: Mum says, «Let's compost the peelings.» What does compost mean here? | Eat the peelings for lunch | *Put the peelings in a heap so they rot | Paint the peelings green | Throw the peelings into the sea
exercise: Which bin is for peelings and leaves? | Glass | General waste | *Compost | Recycling
test: «Frogs and toads spend winter in compost heaps and under logs.» Where do frogs and toads spend winter? | *In compost heaps | In a fridge | On the moon | In the sea
test: Which sentence is true? | Compost is a kind of cloud | *Compost is made from rotted plant and food waste | Compost is always bright blue | Compost is a type of metal
exam: «Worms, fungi and bacteria break kitchen scraps down into rich compost.» Which group are the decomposers in this sentence? | Bees and wasps | Frogs and toads | Dogs and cats | *Worms, fungi and bacteria
